# IP address:
- internet protocol address 
- unique address of a device on the internet
- ex: 89.207.132.170 
- without this computer can't communicate with other computer 


# types of ip address:
1. public ip: assigned by internet service provider (isp) assessible over the internet

2. private ip: used inside a local network


IPv4	               IPv6
32-bit	               128-bit
192.168.1.1  	       2001:db8::1
Limited addresses	   Almost unlimited


#port:
logical endpoint that tells the os which application should receive the request 
ex: Building = IP Address
Apartment = Port


Common Ports
Port	Service
80	    HTTP
443  	HTTPS
3000	React Development
5000	Node.js
8000	Backend APIs
27017	MongoDB



# ip vs port
- ip address identifies the device while port identifies the application/service running on that device 
ex: ip address: 89.207.132.170 port: 3000



